      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "Copyright 2010 Wiley-Liss, Inc.",
        "AbstractText": "We report a critically ill-patient admitted for NSTEMI with acute pulmonary congestion, showing at urgent cardiac catheterization a severely diseased saphenous vein graft as the culprit vessel, with huge atherothrombotic burden. The graft was successfully revascularized by the implantation of 4 M-Guard stent (for proximal to distal) creating a full metal jacket. The M-Guard technology consists on a stainless steel platform wrapped by a micron-level polymer net, that seamlessly expands when the stent is deployed, providing protection from embolic showers."
      },
